    "text": "Value of the Data "
  },
  {
    "source_id": "edbf589d488dc12e86d7e581727db40e76e14633d6731b7774105a6518454e36",
    "path": "competition_agent/assets_raw/dib-2021-107632.pdf",
    "locator": {
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        41.81399917602539,
        174.68386840820312,
        401.5150451660156,
        287.8667297363281
      ],
      "coordinate_system": "PDF points, top-left",
      "line": 1,
      "end_line": 11,
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 838,
      "offset_scope": "block text",
      "block": 4
    },
    "text": "• The dataset is important for validating the mathematical model presented in “Material Ther- \nmal Properties Estimation Via a One-Dimensional Transient Convection Model” [1] . \n• The data are useful for engineers and researchers to establish this method as an alternative \nto current ASTM standards to identify the thermal conductivity. \n• The data can be used to verify other models for heat diffusion in one-dimension. \n• The data can be used to develop a method to test materials with unknown thermal conduc- \ntivity. \n• The data can be used as a comparison with other measurements taken at different facilities. \n• This dataset and model was applied to evaluate the effect of porosity on the thermal per- \nformance in selective laser melted stainless steel additive manufacturing and can be used to \nevaluate other materials [2,5] . "
  },
  {
    "source_id": "edbf589d488dc12e86d7e581727db40e76e14633d6731b7774105a6518454e36",
